7ILfM8","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-01T23:05:21Z","updated_at":"2025-10-01T23:05:21Z","body":"> Could you provide an example usage of this new method?\r\n\r\n@syntaxerror247 I've updated the description with code examples.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358454588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358826679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111135#issuecomment-3358826679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111135","id":3358826679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IM6C3","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T02:45:09Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T02:45:09Z","body":"> * Add overload method for `GodotPlugin#emitSignal(...)` that takes in a `SignalInfo` argument.\r\n>   It's common for `GodotPlugin` implementations to define a set of `SignalInfo` objects to use for registration, then reuse those objects when a signal is emitted. This typically looks like:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> private val EVENT_SIGNAL = SignalInfo(\"event_signal\")\r\n> ...\r\n> override fun getPluginSignals() = setOf(EVENT_SIGNAL)\r\n> ...\r\n> fun dispatchEvent() {\r\n>     emitSignal(EVENT_SIGNAL.name)\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> With this update, the call to emit the signal can be changed to:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> fun dispatchEvent() {\r\n>     emitSignal(EVENT_SIGNAL)\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nHm.. I don't see any use for this overloaded method because you can create string constants for signal names. Eg.\r\n```\r\nprivate val EVENT_SIGNAL = \"event_signal\"\r\noverride fun getPluginSignals() = setOf(SignalInfo(EVENT_SIGNAL))\r\nfun dispatchEvent() {\r\n    emitSignal(EVENT_SIGNAL)\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358826679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358883634","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111135#issuecomment-3358883634","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111135","id":3358883634,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7INH8y","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T03:24:04Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T03:24:04Z","body":"Since you’re working on this, would it be possible to support nullable parameters?\r\nFor ex, I have the following method in my plugin:\r\n```\r\n@UsedByGodot\r\nfun testMethod(param1: String?) {\r\n    if (param1 != null) {\r\n        Log.d(\"godot-test\", param1)\r\n    } else {\r\n        Log.d(\"godot-test\", \"param1 is null\")\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nwhen I call `plugin_singleton.testMethod(null)` from gdscript, it throws an error saying the function doesn’t exist, since it only accepts a string.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3358883634/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3361899142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111135#issuecomment-3361899142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111135","id":3361899142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7IYoKG","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-02T15:35:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-02T15:35:31Z","body":"> Since you’re working on this, would it be possible to support nullable parameters?\n> For ex, I have the following method in my plugin:\n> ```\n> @UsedByGodot\n> fun testMethod(param1: String?) {\n>     if (param1 != null) {\n>         Log.d(\"godot-test\", param1)\n>     } else {\n>         Log.d(\"godot-test\", \"param1 is null\")\n>     }\n> }\n> ```\n> when I call `plugin_singleton.testMethod(null)` from gdscript, it throws an error saying the function doesn’t exist, since it only accepts a string.\n\nYeah I can take a look!\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3361899142/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3366165910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111135#issuecomment-3366165910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111135","id":3366165910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Io52W","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-03T15:21:36Z","updated_at":"2025-10-03T15:21:36Z","body":"> Since you’re working on this, would it be possible to support nullable parameters? For ex, I have the following method in my plugin:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> @UsedByGodot\r\n> fun testMethod(param1: String?) {\r\n>     if (param1 != null) {\r\n>         Log.d(\"godot-test\", param1)\r\n>     } else {\r\n>         Log.d(\"godot-test\", \"param1 is null\")\r\n>     }\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> when I call `plugin_singleton.testMethod(null)` from gdscript, it throws an error saying the function doesn’t exist, since it only accepts a string.\r\n\r\n@syntaxerror247 I thought on it some more, and I think it's better to keep the current limitation in place for a few reasons:\r\n- It aligns with gdscript type system. The limitation you mention only applies to `String` and `Callable` which matches gdscript static typing when it's enabled. E.g: A `String` variable in gdscript cannot be assigned `null` when static typing is enabled.\r\n-  Removing this limitation would be fine when interacting with Java code, but would be an issue when interacting with Kotlin code. From the gdscript side, we can't tell when a `String` argument to a Kotlin method is a nullable `String` or a non-nullable `String`. As such the safe approach is to assume that it's a non-nullable `String` and prevent passing `null` because the developer has control over the gdscript code and can modify it to accommodate the limitation (e.g: passing an empty string instead), whereas the Kotlin side can be a third-party library that's unable to be modified, where passing a `null` value could cause a runtime `NullPointerException`.\r\n- Last, as Kotlin and gdscript demonstrate, pushing for null-safety is a safer, more robust approach to development, so we should encourage that approach whenever possible (e.g: passing empty string instead of null values).\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3366165910/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3429409615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111135#issuecomment-3429409615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111135","id":3429409615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MaKNP","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T20:16:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T20:16:52Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3429409615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]